2025-07-08 18:11:09,126 [scheduling-1] INFO  c.s.service.GptSentimentAnalyzer - Analyze sentiment for symbol: AAPL with text:$meta Is way ahead of $aapl now In fashology  
 
Meta just bought nearly a 3% stake in EssilorLuxottica, the world’s largest eyewear company and owner of Ray-Ban and Oakley, in a deal worth about $3.5 billion. Bloomberg reports Meta could increase its stake to 5% over time.  
 
This deepens their partnership as Meta ramps up its AI smart glasses push, aiming to control hardware and distribution instead of relying on smartphones built by competitors. EssilorLuxottica gets a stronger foothold in tech if Meta’s AR bets pay off.
